  "notes": "Release date 2025-07-31 printed on the official research blog ('July 31th, 2025 … Today, we are releasing: Step3'); open-source under Apache 2.0 (GitHub repo created 2025-07-25T03:11Z, matching the 2025-07-25 launch event). System tech report: arXiv 2507.19427. The Overall Performance table is DOM machine-readable; Step 3's own column (no asterisk) is vendor-reported and transcribed as 11 verified rows. Table note verbatim: '* means reproduced performance using the same settings' — competitor columns without * are cited from those models' official results and with * are StepFun's same-setting reproductions; competitor columns (Llama 4 Maverick, ERNIE 4.5-thinking, QvQ-72B, GLM-4.1V-thinking, MiMo-VL, DeepSeek R1-0528, MiniMax-M1-80k, Qwen3-235B-A22B-Thinking(-2507), o3, Claude Opus 4/Sonnet 4 thinking, Gemini 2.5 Pro/Flash, Grok 4) are recorded here in notes only, not as rows. Gemini 2.5 Flash footnote: results may be lower than real performance due to insufficient instruction following. The GitHub README Evaluation Results section is an image (step3_bmk.jpeg) — the blog DOM table is the machine-readable source of the same numbers. 2026-09-01 audit (accessibility): from this network the primary blog URL 302-redirects to chat.stepfun.com/unavailable-in-region (region gate; both curl and a second fetch path agree), matching the archive manifest status \"inaccessible\". All 11 Step 3 values were independently CONFIRMED against the official GitHub repo figure github.com/stepfun-ai/Step3 -> figures/step3_bmk.jpeg (downloaded and read 2026-09-01): MMMU 74.2, MATH-Vision 64.8, SimpleVQA 62.2, HallusionBench 64.2, ZeroBench(sub) 23.0, DYNMATH 50.1, AIME25 82.9, GPQA-Diamond 73.0, LiveCodeBench(202408-202505) 67.1, HMMT25 70.0, CNMO24 83.7; the figure contains no additional Step 3 rows, so traversal is complete. primary_sources[0] stays the official dated blog (it is the announcement; its content is preserved in the archive manifest notes and mirrored by the official repo)."
